replace('archive/07-technical-architecture/spatial-world-runtime.md','Respect the existing fixed-step order and time-debt policy; do not introduce a second simulation clock.','Respect start/end interval ownership and actual-progress debt accounting in [simulation time](../../docs/simulation-time.md); do not introduce a second simulation clock.')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','Preserve one-second native semantics,', '''[Simulation time](simulation-time.md) owns the elapsed-integration contract. Compile participant IDs outside drafts and reuse them until a membership/component-changing command invalidates that roster; retain IDs rather than draft entities. The current finite native families capture active rates/work at the start and integrate to a relevant mechanical or authored fidelity boundary, instead of traversing the world once per game second. Status applicability and immutable static-object exposure reuse remove unrelated work. Ordering, saved randomness, real collision and source-scoped evidence remain protected, but the obsolete one-second trace is not itself a gameplay requirement. The [base time policy](worlds/base/time.md) states sampling/approximation limits and coupled-rule fallbacks.''')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','- Finalize a bounded set of fixed steps once', '- Bound finalization and work using the existing elapsed-interval owner. Do not merely pass a larger duration into a legacy per-second implementation: active rates, starts/completions, consequences, observation fidelity and RNG ordering need explicit contracts. PF13 delivers the current finite families; arbitrary coupled mechanics and regional schedules remain gated.')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','Native throughput must cover 60 one-second transitions', '''Measure actual game-time progress divided by real elapsed time against `baseRatio × speed`, with headroom for commands, persistence and publication. There is no sixty/480-transition requirement. Count actual completed intervals, their game durations and CPU cost separately; a short deadline can still dominate a global scheduler. Preserve immutable snapshot sharing, append lineage and privacy invalidation. Measure initial exposure/freezing and mature-state growth, not only short pre-frozen runs.''')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','Action acceptance and first visible movement are different milestones.', '''Action acceptance and first visible movement are different milestones. The current fifty-millisecond host wake admits elapsed time and publishes scoped progress without imposing that rate on rendering. Retain one-real-second routine durability and immediate consequential/authorization boundaries. Future pose coalescing must preserve reliable events and cannot advance unowed time. Device-paced interpolation and prediction are separate presentation/network choices, not simulation tick requirements.''')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','The current host has a base ratio of 60 simulated seconds', '''The base conversion is sixty game seconds per real second: speed eight requests 480 game seconds of progress, **not 480 mandatory native transitions**. Use [the elapsed-interval contract](simulation-time.md), not the superseded 2.08 ms per-one-second-step assumption. The host retains an approximately eight-millisecond cooperative work budget, while a single atomic interval may exceed it. Measure actual achieved clock rate, interval count/duration, work per affected entity, command latency and debt together. Rendering targets display cadence independently; no twenty-FPS cap follows from sparse updates.''')
replace('docs/performance.md','or replace several fixed steps with a single coarse step to meet the target','or jump over unhandled consequential boundaries to meet the target')
replace('docs/performance.md','fixed-step yielding and trigger-based background work','elapsed-prefix yielding and trigger-based background work')
paragraph('docs/performance.md','Move genuinely cold historical data off repeated', '''Move genuinely cold historical data off repeated finalization/serialization paths under PF08 while retaining evidence, stable IDs, pending commitments, current knowledge and explicit durable reads. PF13 already integrates selected finite rates to their next bound; it does not certify arbitrary nonlinear or coupled authored rules. Use the [running boundary catalogue](maintainers/simulation-boundaries.md) to identify further independent deadlines, valid bounds and invalidators before adding regional schedules or a general event heap. Do not discard meaningful interactions to make a latency target pass.''')
replace('docs/maintainers/performance.md','preserve one writer and fixed-step order','preserve one writer and native phase order')
paragraph('docs/maintainers/performance.md','- [ ] Verify backlog backpressure stops simulation growth', '- [ ] Qualify nonblocking memory pressure with recent/protected evidence, failed or unavailable maintenance and mature histories. Preserve sources and allow native time/movement; real storage errors still pause admission. Failed unchanged maintenance must not retry automatically. Profile retained-history traversal before increasing workload claims. This supersedes the obsolete request to stop simulation on optional memory backlog.')
paragraph('docs/maintainers/performance.md','- [ ] **PF12.3 /', '- [ ] **PF12.3 / PF09 / EPR02–03** Complete dirty region/target updates and broader static-exposure qualification. The immutable static-object exposure helper and unchanged episode reuse are delivered within PF13; do not reimplement them. Preserve source-scoped names, capability/geometry invalidation and complete outputs; never retain draft entities.')
paragraph('docs/maintainers/performance.md','Dense 8x is not complete.', 'Extreme-density 8x remains unqualified. PF13 supersedes the assumed one-game-second stepping requirement; current elapsed measurements are not interchangeable with the historical fixed-step baseline. Continue regional/event-bound work, sensory indexing and history/render attribution without weakening meaningful effects or hiding debt.')
append('docs/maintainers/performance.md', '''## PF13 — Elapsed-time simulation

[Simulation time](../simulation-time.md) owns the engine contract; [base time](../worlds/base/time.md) owns bundled fidelity and [the boundary catalogue](simulation-boundaries.md) records future candidates. [Evidence](../verification/elapsed-simulation.md) separates executed diagnostics from unqualified scale and semantic coverage. This is not a second scheduler, physics engine or persistence program.

- [x] **PF13.1** Separate game-clock conversion, host integration opportunities, pose publication and device-paced rendering. Replace mandatory one-game-second iteration with bounded actual elapsed progress and retain unadvanced debt.
- [x] **PF13.2** Reconcile due start transitions, capture active status/native rates and working-action identity, integrate only their valid interval, then apply completion/status/perception outcomes. Preserve ordered commands, depletion/conservation and no retroactive work. Unsupported coupled/clamped families retain a documented fallback.
- [x] **PF13.3** Compose finite bounds for capacity/concern/needs, status comparisons/daily windows, work/supply, route/support waypoints, flight waits/landing/falling and conversation/commitment deadlines. Keep world policy outside universal engine assumptions; no model call or durable SDK object is introduced.
- [x] **PF13.4** Reuse conservative status applicability, immutable static-object exposure and unchanged episode membership. Preserve current-main physical contact and nonblocking memory pressure. Do not create duplicate owners when the speech branch is integrated.
- [x] **PF13.5** Fix start-boundary takeoff contact, numerical waypoint residue and pathological immediate blocked-flight retry through the existing saved wait. Five-game-second shared retry boundaries are revisitable bundled policy, not fair crowd arbitration. Keep underside/occupancy checks.
- [x] **PF13.6** Run actual finite-boundary, HTTP movement/pause/restart and 8x native/server stress observations. Record the dense contested-flight failure alongside near-target ordinary mixed-world results; no unlimited-capacity or physical-GPU claim.
- [x] **PF13.7** Read the current speech branch, preserve its ownership and post integration guidance on PR #3. Land/reconcile elapsed integration before combining its one-second snapshot batching; keep dB listener evidence and real-time captions. The combined branch is not yet qualified.
- [ ] **PF13.8** Qualify independent variable-partition/coupled-flow, simultaneous resource depletion, zero-time chains, threshold equality, fractional save/cursor handling and start/end event ordering. Cross-layer automated scenarios are SR27–SR31 in TODO; existing valid cases remain.
- [ ] **PF13.9** Replace global-minimum coupling only when a concrete region/participant scheduler can prove dependency and invalidation coverage. The contested-perch workload currently fails 8x. Profile local due queues, dirty sensing, blocked-landing occupancy wakeups and retained-history costs; do not solve it by moving fewer legitimate actors or changing clock speed.
- [ ] **PF13.10** Qualify richer swept perception/contact boundaries and unknown authored rate dependencies. Current one-metre sampling can miss short peeks/tangencies and relative motion; physical interaction admission is not proof of complete continuous awareness.
- [ ] **PF13.11** Run the joined hearing/elapsed stack with actual emissions, history, cognition scheduling and captions; qualify event-time snapshots, pause/load/source revocation and sustained frame/command tails. Caption time and rendering remain independent of acceleration.

Stop rule: prefer bounded elapsed families and explicit limitations over an unused generic event framework. A discovered natural deadline belongs in the catalogue with its invalidators and owner; it does not become implemented merely because it is listed.''')
